From 8ab24daee9c641634fda5cac30389ad4b2cfda5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Wed Sep 30 19:26:28 2026 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Merge windows-release: cheaper GX worker draws, thread timing, cache folder

The Windows build's RecompCore work since 6892947 (e8c2bb3, f93c05f, 2a85bd1,
825f103, 4f7a3ec, 82607d4): the derived pipeline state cached by a register
version, no assembly totals walk, the last pipeline lookup and bind group
reused, Smooth Motion jobs without a copy for repeated constants and with a
fence only when the helper may sleep; constant blocks compared against a copy
off Apple GPUs; gather-pipe writes as a run of bytes; DOL_AURORA_CACHE_DIR;
the stall watchdog on Mac and Linux only; graphics threads' CPU time and slow
presents in the log.

With save states: a register state put back from a state takes a fresh
derived-cache version (GxCoreState::renew_version), since the saved one
belongs to the run that saved it. On an M3 Max, Outset's spawn view at Smooth
Motion 60: the FIFO worker 55.4 -> 53.2 percent busy, 95.6 percent of draws
hitting the derived cache, and DOL_GXCORE_DERIVED_VERIFY=1 finds no mismatch
in 5.7 M hits on a walk nor in 7.0 M after a save state load.

